=== layout: section

# Shark Tank

## Oct 22, 2026
## Slides due six hours before class

=== layout: one-panel

# Shark Tank

@body

- Choice of Presentation Order based on When you turn in the One Great Idea Form
- Each student gets 4 minutes to present
  - I will try to enforce time, questions are allowed to go over <some>.
- Present the problem and your solution.
  - Goal\: to recruit other students to join your project.
- [I sent you a Google Slides link]{color=red}, so you can work on them up until your presentation begins.
  - Slides are due six hours before class; use the current Blackboard submission instructions.

=== layout: one-panel

# Pre-Recorded Videos

@body

- Pre-recorded videos are [ALLOWED]{color=green}.
- Use your own voice and follow the presentation guidelines.
- Four-minute target; 3 minutes 36 seconds to 4 minutes 24 seconds.
- Upload to YouTube or Blackboard under Assignments.
- Submit six hours before your scheduled presentation class.
- Complete the title and reference slides in the class template.
- Put the video link on slide 2 so Dr. Voss can download it.

=== layout: one-panel

# Shark Tank Suggested Format

@body

- 1. Title: your name, company, and product.
- 2. Problem: who or what is affected?
- 3. Scale: why does the problem matter?
- 4. Solution: what will your company make?
- 5. Science: how does the biotechnology work?
- 6. Competition: why is your approach better?
- 7. Thanks and references.
- [You may use a different order if it tells a clear story.]{color=red}

=== layout: one-panel

# Questions to Think About

@body

- What is it?
- How does it work?
- When is it used?
- What will it accomplish?
- When should it not be used?

=== layout: one-panel
hidden: true

# Shark Tanks Slides MUST\:

@body

- [Use the Google Slides TEMPLATE link provided to you.]{color=red}
- 7 OR LESS slides total
  - [I will delete slide #8 if you have one!!!]{color=red}
- Include a title page with your name and your company name in clean text.

@notes

